From ee72402534f6eea38d54eb4011eb3baa3ed48ddc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Brendan Lynskey <brendanlynskey@googlemail.com>
Date: Sat, 28 Nov 2026 10:13:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 8/8] hw/riscv: add the brv32p-linux machine and CPU

The brv32p-linux machine is the BRV32P SoC with the smallest set of additions
that Linux needs, to settle what a Linux-capable RTL must gain. The CPU is the
brv32p with the A extension, S and U modes, Sv32 and the cycle, time and
instret counters with their high halves; it keeps the custom extensions and
the misaligned-access trap, and has no PMP. The machine adds an ACLINT in the
layout of the SiFive CLINT at 0x20010000 and 128 MiB of RAM at 0x80000000,
decoded fully, and keeps the boot SRAM at 0 and the GPIO, UART and timer where
the RTL has them. The firmware, kernel, initramfs and device tree are loaded
as for the virt machine. -M brv32p is unchanged.

Signed-off-by: Brendan Lynskey <brendanlynskey@googlemail.com>

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
